    body: "JEE Main (NTA)",
    help: "For JEE Main 2025, NTA's notice as reported by Careers360 on 25 October 2024 gave candidates with benchmark disabilities a minimum of one extra hour on the three-hour paper, and at least 20 minutes per hour when a scribe is used. A scribe is automatic for blindness, locomotor disability and cerebral palsy. For other categories you need a government medical certificate stating a limitation in writing.",
    note: "That wording means a candidate with dyslexia may get extra time without getting a scribe. Read the bulletin of the year you sit.",
  },
  {
    body: "CLAT (law entrance)",
    help: "The CLAT 2024 notification gave candidates with a benchmark disability 40 extra minutes on the two-hour paper, for 2 hours 40 minutes in all. A scribe is allowed for blindness, locomotor disability affecting both arms and cerebral palsy, and for others with a certified limitation that impedes writing. A scribe cannot be linked to a coaching centre.",
