  },
  {
    body: "ICSI (Company Secretary)",
    help: "The ICSI FAQ lists dyslexia, dysgraphia and dyscalculia as special cases. The concessions named are leniency on spelling mistakes, a cover-page stamp and instructions to the examiner. The FAQ does not explicitly grant a scribe or extra time for these, though it gives 20 extra minutes per hour to listed physical and sensory disabilities. Apply in writing at least 45 days before the exam.",
    note: "The FAQ shows no date, so confirm with ICSI before you plan around it. Other professional bodies set their own rules.",
  },
  {
    body: "Government recruitment exams",
    help: "DEPwD's memorandum of 10 August 2022 sets compensatory time of not less than 20 minutes per hour of examination and allows a scribe for candidates with a certificate of limitation in writing. Persons with 40 percent or more fall under separate DEPwD guidelines dated 29 August 2018.",
    note: "Each recruiter's notice says how to apply. Send the certificate at the time of the form, not at the centre.",
  },
];

const taskRows = [
