    grow: "One subject or one learner group, a recognised qualification, then workshops and private sessions.",
  },
  {
    n: "06",
    name: "Hospitality, events and operations",
    scale: "mid",
    why: "These roles run on people, speed and judgment in the moment. Many tasks are done on the floor, not on paper.",
    pays: "Hotels, restaurants, event firms, logistics and retail companies.",
    trust: "Reliability, guest reviews, a supervisor reference and a record of events or shifts handled well.",
    watch: "Rosters, reports and shift logs are written, so use checklists and ask for templates. Shifts and stamina matter, so check the weekly reality first.",
    grow: "Move toward supervision, sales, revenue or your own events business.",
  },
  {
    n: "07",
    name: "Law, finance and accounting",
    scale: "mid",
    why: "These careers reward careful thinking, and some people with dyslexia do well with the right tools. They are also the most reading, spelling and number heavy, so go in with open eyes.",
    pays: "Law firms and companies, accounting and advisory firms, and clients through your own practice.",
    trust: "Internships, written samples that have been checked, a reference from a senior, and a clean record of exam results.",
    watch: "Professional bodies differ on exam help: the ICSI FAQ names spelling leniency, not a scribe, for learning disabilities. Long reading loads and number-heavy papers add up, so check the exam help before you enrol.",
