  <h2 id="tools-ai">Tools and AI: what they fix and what they do not</h2>

  <div class="split-grid">
    <div class="split-card split-card--grow">
      <div class="split-card__label">What tools can fix</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Text-to-speech turns long reading into listening.</li>
        <li>Voice typing and spell-check turn speech into clean drafts.</li>
        <li>Spreadsheets and calculators take over arithmetic.</li>
        <li>AI assistants can summarise a document, rewrite an email and explain a formula.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="split-card split-card--risk">
      <div class="split-card__label">What to watch</div>
      <ul>
        <li>AI can be wrong. Check every number, name and date before you send it.</li>
        <li>Keep medical and assessment reports out of public tools.</li>
        <li>Routine writing and summarising are the tasks AI is taking over, so build skills beyond them.</li>
        <li>Tools in the exam hall must be approved. Practise only with what is allowed.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    A staged path: start now with one reading tool and one writing tool you use every day. Later, as
    tools improve, learn to check their output and to design a small workflow, so you direct the
    tool. Combine deep skill in your field, clear communication and AI use, with proof others can see.
  </p>

  <h2 id="school-college">Class 9 to college: choices that keep options open</h2>

  <h3>In school</h3>

  <p>
    Start the paperwork before the board exam year. Ask the school for its concession process, keep
    teacher notes and remedial records, and find out which subjects test through projects and which
    through one written paper. A stream that suits how you show knowledge usually beats a stream
    chosen for status.
  </p>

  <h3>Choosing a college and course</h3>

  <p>
    Ask in writing before you pay a fee. The answers tell you more than a brochure.
  </p>

  <ul class="check-list">
    <li>Will the college accept your SLD certificate for extra time, a scribe or a laptop in internal exams?</li>
    <li>Does it have a student support or disability cell, and who runs it?</li>
    <li>Can you record lectures or get notes in advance?</li>
    <li>How much of the grade comes from projects, practicals and presentations, and how much from one written paper?</li>
    <li>What did past students with learning disabilities do after the course?</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Government and aided colleges must keep not less than 5 percent of seats for benchmark
    disabilities under Section 32. A seat is only the start, so a college with real support can beat
    a famous one without it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="at-work">At work: interviews and reasonable adjustments</h2>

  <h3>What to ask for</h3>

  <p>
    Adjustments are usually small and cheap. Common ones are written instructions with a short spoken
    walk-through, voice typing and spell-check switched on, templates for repeat emails, extra time
    for timed tests, and documents sent a day ahead. Name the one or two that help you most and
    offer to confirm in writing.
  </p>

  <h3>Interviews and tests</h3>

  <p>
    Ask what the process is before you attend. If there is a timed written test, ask for extra time or
    a different format, and lead with your portfolio so the conversation starts from finished work.
  </p>

  <h3>What the law says</h3>

  <p>
    The legal points on reasonable accommodation, equal opportunity policies and when to tell an
    employer are in our guide to
    <a href="/blog/career-options/career-options-for-students-with-disabilities-india/">career options for students with disabilities</a>.
    It is not a promise for private jobs, so ask in writing and keep copies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="money">College money</h2>

  <p>
    Plan the family's education money before you pick a college. Keep the degree fee to roughly a
    tenth of the total, which is a working rule of thumb and not a research result. If the pot is 10
    lakh rupees, about 1 lakh goes to the degree.
  </p>

  <p>
    The balance covers a laptop, reading and writing
    software, a formal assessment, remedial sessions and the projects that build your portfolio. When a
    college wants nearer a fifth of the pot, ask what it gives that no cheaper option does, for
    example a licence the profession legally demands. Borrowing for a degree is a last resort.
  </p>

  <p>
    A certified SLD is a benchmark disability, so look at the DEPwD scholarships described in the
    disabilities guide above, and confirm income limits and dates on scholarships.gov.in.
  </p>

  <p>
    Plenty of
    skills can be learned free or cheaply. Before paying for any course, look at what the teacher has
    shipped lately, whether the material is current, whether you get feedback on practice work and where
    earlier students ended up. A certificate on its own proves little.
  </p>

  <p class="note-line">
    Everything numeric above is a rule or scheme detail taken from official papers on 30 October
    2026. None of it is a pay forecast, and we print no salary band because we found no dependable
    source for these routes. Read live vacancies and ask people in the job.
  </p>

